{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"The water cycle: evaporation and condensation","theme":{"background":"#e8f4fb","foreground":"#1a3a52","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Evaporation"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Evaporation is when liquid water turns into water vapour, a gas, when it is heated, usually by the sun."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Condensation"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Condensation is when water vapour cools and turns back into tiny liquid water droplets, such as clouds forming in the sky."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What does the sun do to water in a puddle?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Heats it so it evaporates","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Freezes it into ice","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Turns it into soil","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Where does condensation usually happen in the water cycle?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"In clouds, when vapour cools","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Under the ground, when it rains","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Only in the sea, at night","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"On which day would a wet puddle dry up fastest?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"A warm, sunny day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"A cold, frosty day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"A cold, windless day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Ava left her wet coat on the line. It is a hot, sunny day. What should she do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Hang it in the sun","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Hang it in the shade","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The sun heats the water and it evaporates quickly. The coat is dry by lunchtime!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"In the shade it stays cool, so the water evaporates slowly. The coat takes all afternoon to dry."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Why does warm air help water evaporate faster?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Heat gives water particles more energy to escape as vapour","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Warm air makes water heavier so it sinks","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Warm air stops water from moving","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which step of the water cycle turns vapour into clouds?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Condensation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Evaporation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Freezing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the water cycle lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how evaporation and condensation work, and why warm days dry things faster."}],"actions":[]}}
